  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#13035\", \"PowerToys#9496\", \"PowerToys#15125\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys has no built-in tool that dims inactive windows. The earlier tickets were merged into PowerToys#13035, which is the main one to follow. Add a 👍 to it and put your multi-monitor and adjustable-intensity requirements there instead of opening a new request. In that thread the maintainers suggested building it as a separate proof-of-concept app first. The design they discussed was an underlay with a configurable colour and transparency, activated by a hotkey. A community project, PowerDimmer (github.com/[user]/PowerDimmer), was shared in that thread and does something similar. Until PowerToys adds this, you could try it.\"}",
